om2
note compiler/gate.om: the gate of compiler/si.om, in pure seeded Omega.
note
note Build and run from the repository root, with the pinned seeded compiler and an existing
note scratch directory WORK:
note   "$OMC" < compiler/gate.om > WORK/gate && chmod +x WORK/gate && WORK/gate "$OMC" WORK
note It checks that OMC is the pinned omc by its sha256 (any other omc, or none: SI NOT_RUN, exit 3),
note builds si from compiler/si.om and links from compiler/links.om with it into WORK/si and
note WORK/links, then runs twenty-six cases:
note   1 the committed inputs regenerate README.md and repos.tsv byte-identically (exit 0)
note   2 head mutant: the last digit of the first inventory row's head moved on by one is refused
note   3 RID mutant: the last character of the first inventory row's RID changed is refused
note   4 the stale inventory of commit 3c37e6fb (compiler/gate-3c37e6fb.tsv) is refused
note   5 links on the repository root passes: every link row valid, no project source vendored
note   6 link RID mutant: WORK/5-tree/repos.tsv, the first link row's RID ending in 0 (not base58),
note     is refused by links
note   7 link crypto mutant: WORK/6-tree/repos.tsv, the first link row's RID starting rad:z2ft64
note     (the withdrawn crypto project), is refused by links
note   8 vendored mutant: WORK/7-tree, the committed repos.tsv beside a planted project directory
note     omega-mv holding main.om, is refused by links
note   9 minimal tree: WORK/A-tree, the committed repos.tsv and compiler/ holding only its eight
note     allowed file names (empty), passes links; cases 10-26 each change one thing in it
note  10-20 link-row mutants of WORK/B-tree to WORK/L-tree/repos.tsv, each refused by links with
note     its own message: the first link row's name Omega-Pearl and aien-CRYPTO-mv (withdrawn
note     crypto, any case) and ../x (bad name); its head with capitals, with a g, and 41 digits;
note     its tier Core; its RID with a 29th character, and rad:z then 28 z (more than 20 bytes);
note     the header's first field nam; and the header with no row after it
note  21-26 planted entries, each refused by links as not an SI file: compiler/evil.om (WORK/M-tree),
note     compiler/si.om as a symbolic link to gate.om (N), a root symbolic link lnk to compiler (O),
note     a root file evil.rs (P), a root directory vendor (Q) and gpu/x.bin (R)
note The si mutants are written to WORK/head.tsv and WORK/rid.tsv. Cases 2-4, 6, 7 and 10-20 first
note check that the input's sha256 differs from the committed file's, and cases 8 and 21-26 that the
note planted entry exists, so an edit that did not apply cannot pass as a refusal. An si refusal
note must be exit 1, stderr starting "si: " and the expected message, the README copy unchanged and
note no repos.tsv written; a links refusal exit 1 and stderr starting "links: " and the expected
note message; links passing exit 0 and stdout starting "links: pass: ". Each case prints PASS or
note FAIL with the evidence, then "SI pass=N fail=M"; exit 0 when no case fails, 1 otherwise, 2 on
note a usage error. links reads a directory entry's kind from getdents64 and refuses DT_UNKNOWN,
note which no case plants: ext4 and tmpfs never return it.
note SHA-256 (fn kinit to fn finish) is copied unchanged from omega-mv om/sha256/sha256-om2.om
note at f4df82394e35893dcf1354dda69a2fe028d94bc1 (Apache-2.0, FIPS 180-4).

